{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Object Selection.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Object Selection.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"object selection object selection","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Object Selection.md","fileName":"Object Selection.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Object Selection","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Spatial Interaction]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Interaction","3D Manipulation","Depth Cue","Progressive Refinement","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Object Selection.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Object Selection.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"object selection object selection","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Object Selection.md","fileName":"Object Selection.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Object Selection","heading":"Object Selection","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Object selection is the task of acquiring or identifying one object or a subset of objects from the available set. It is also called target acquisition and is a canonical [[3D Manipulation]] task.\n\nSelection difficulty depends on target size and distance, object density, occlusion, number of targets, input precision, and the [[Depth Cue]]s provided by the display. Pointing techniques often perform well for remote selection, while grasping techniques are generally more suitable for subsequent manipulation.\n\nDense scenes can use [[Progressive Refinement]]: a coarse first action narrows the candidates and a simpler second action identifies the final target.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Interaction","3D Manipulation","Depth Cue","Progressive Refinement","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"